{"name":"Stag Beetle","hex":"#603b41","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"stag beetle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of numerous large beetles of the family Lucanidae, the males having elaborate mandibles resembling the antlers of a stag\nespecially, the largest beetle in the UK, of species Lucanus cervus.","especially, the largest beetle in the UK, of species Lucanus cervus."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stag_beetle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Stag beetle","blocks":[{"text":"Stag beetles compose the family Lucanidae. It has about 1,200 species of beetles in four subfamilies. Some species grow to over 12 centimetres, but most to about 5 cm (2 in)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Golden_stag_beetle.jpg/330px-Golden_stag_beetle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stag_beetle"},{"title":"Deer","blocks":[{"text":"A deer or true deer is a hoofed ruminant ungulate of the family Cervidae. Cervidae is divided into subfamilies Cervinae and Capreolinae. Male deer of almost all species, as well as female reindeer, grow and shed new antlers each year. These antlers are bony extensions of the skull and are often used for combat between males."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Family_Cervidae_five_species.jpg/330px-Family_Cervidae_five_species.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deer"},{"title":"Beetle","blocks":[{"text":"Beetles are insects that form the order Coleoptera, in the superorder Holometabola. Their front pair of wings are hardened into wing-cases, elytra, distinguishing them from most other insects. The Coleoptera, with about 400,000 described species, is the largest of all orders, constituting almost 40% of described arthropods and 25% of all known animal species; new species are discovered frequently, with estimates suggesting that there are between 0.9 and 2.1 million total species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Coleoptera_collage.png/330px-Coleoptera_collage.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beetle"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Dorcus_curvidens_hopei_sjh.jpg/500px-Dorcus_curvidens_hopei_sjh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Dorcus_curvidens_hopei_sjh.jpg/500px-Dorcus_curvidens_hopei_sjh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dorcus curvidens male (left) and female (right)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADorcus_curvidens_hopei_sjh.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/COLE_Lucanidae_Lissotes.png/500px-COLE_Lucanidae_Lissotes.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/COLE_Lucanidae_Lissotes.png/1280px-COLE_Lucanidae_Lissotes.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/COLE_Lucanidae_Lissotes.png/500px-COLE_Lucanidae_Lissotes.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Paralissotes sp. illustrated by Des Helmore","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACOLE_Lucanidae_Lissotes.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Metopodontus_savagei-Mus%C3%A9e_royal_de_l%27Afrique_centrale.jpg/500px-Metopodontus_savagei-Mus%C3%A9e_royal_de_l%27Afrique_centrale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Metopodontus_savagei-Mus%C3%A9e_royal_de_l%27Afrique_ce